<section class="card panel"><div class="load-head"><h3>Pending review load</h3><span id="loadValue" class="load-value"></span></div><div class="load-track"><i id="loadBar"></i></div><div id="ledger" class="ledger"></div><div id="history" class="history"></div><div class="history-note">Observed load · dashed threshold · blue lines mark accepted reinterpretations.</div><p class="history-note">Released load means reduced local discrepancy. Shape-reference error remains a separate measure.</p></section>
<section class="card panel"><h3>Local proposal review</h3><div id="reviewMeta" class="review-meta"></div><div id="reviews"></div></section><section class="card panel"><h3>What to look for</h3><ul id="notes" class="notes"></ul><details id="evidence"><summary>Recorded transition evidence</summary><ul id="events" class="events"></ul></details></section></aside></div>
<details class="explanation"><summary>Scope and accounting</summary><ul id="summary"></ul><p>Values are diagnostics in selected coordinate/load bases. They are not confidence scores or a physical energy model. Construction definitions, response fractions, thresholds and candidate libraries are authored; the reviews and their timing follow the observed state.</p></details>
